\paragraph{Where the advantage manifests.}
The advantage appears entirely at evaluation (PPL 17.65 vs.\ 17.69 on human-authored text); unweighted training loss curves overlap (${\sim}1.4\%$ difference), consistent with reshaping the effective distribution without changing the optimization trajectory.
Adaptive $\bstar$ (17.653) matches Golden Ratio weighting (17.654) without oracle access to $\rho$.

\paragraph{Connection to convergence theory.}
\citet{wang2026survive} prove that convergence rate scales with the effective real fraction $\alpha$; our $\tau$ sets a floor on this quantity per batch.
Their analysis assumes known contamination proportion, whereas ours estimates quality from detector scores---$\tau$ is thus an empirical hyperparameter with theoretical motivation, and deriving it from first principles remains open.

